    "cellCounter": 28,
    "cells": [
      {
        "id": 1,
        "code": "# Tutoriel d'arbre généalogique avec UnifyWeaver\n\nCe carnet interactif montre comment utiliser UnifyWeaver pour compiler des prédicats Prolog en scripts Bash.\n\n## Prérequis\n\n- SWI-Prolog installé\n- Bibliothèque UnifyWeaver disponible\n- Noyau Jupyter Prolog installé (`pip install prolog-jupyter-kernel`)\n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage\n\nÀ la fin de ce carnet, vous saurez :\n1. Définir des faits et règles Prolog\n2. Utiliser UnifyWeaver pour compiler des prédicats en Bash\n3. Tester les scripts Bash générés\n4. Comprendre la compilation de fermeture transitive",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 2,
        "code": "## Étape 1 : Initialiser l'environnement UnifyWeaver\n\nTout d'abord, nous devons charger les modules UnifyWeaver. Nous utiliserons le fichier `init.pl` du répertoire education.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 3,
        "code": "% Charger le fichier d'initialisation\n['../init'].",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Cannot find file: ../init",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Cannot find file: ../init</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 4,
        "code": "## Étape 2 : Définir les relations familiales\n\nDéfinissons quelques relations parent-enfant à partir de l'arbre généalogique biblique.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 5,
        "code": "% Définir les faits parent\n:- dynamic parent/2.\n\nparent(abraham, isaac).\nparent(abraham, ishmael).\nparent(isaac, jacob).\nparent(isaac, esau).\nparent(jacob, reuben).\nparent(jacob, simeon).\nparent(jacob, levi).\nparent(jacob, judah).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 6,
        "code": "## Étape 3 : Tester les requêtes de parenté\n\nAvant de compiler, vérifions que nos données sont correctes à l'aide de quelques requêtes Prolog.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 7,
        "code": "% Requête : Qui sont les enfants d'Abraham ?\nparent(abraham, Child).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Child = isaac\nChild = ishmael",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Child = isaac\nChild = ishmael</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 8,
        "code": "% Requête : Qui sont les enfants de Jacob ?\nparent(jacob, Child).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Child = reuben\nChild = simeon\nChild = levi\nChild = judah",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Child = reuben\nChild = simeon\nChild = levi\nChild = judah</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 9,
        "code": "## Étape 4 : Définir la relation d'ancêtre\n\nDéfinissons maintenant la fermeture transitive — la relation `ancestor`.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 10,
        "code": "% Définir ancestor comme la fermeture transitive de parent\n:- dynamic ancestor/2.\n\n% Cas de base : un parent est un ancêtre\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\n\n% Cas récursif : si X est le parent de Y et Y est l'ancêtre de Z, alors X est l'ancêtre de Z\nancestor(X, Z) :- parent(X, Y), ancestor(Y, Z).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 11,
        "code": "## Étape 5 : Tester les requêtes d'ancêtre\n\nVérifions que notre prédicat d'ancêtre fonctionne correctement.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 12,
        "code": "% Requête : Abraham est-il un ancêtre de Jacob ?\n( ancestor(abraham, jacob) ->\n    writeln('Yes: Abraham is an ancestor of Jacob')\n;\n    writeln('No: Abraham is not an ancestor of Jacob')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Yes: Abraham is an ancestor of Jacob",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Yes: Abraham is an ancestor of Jacob</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 13,
        "code": "% Requête : Quels sont tous les descendants d'Abraham ?\nancestor(abraham, Descendant).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "Descendant = isaac\nDescendant = ishmael\nDescendant = jacob\nDescendant = esau\nDescendant = reuben\nDescendant = simeon\nDescendant = levi\nDescendant = judah",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">Descendant = isaac\nDescendant = ishmael\nDescendant = jacob\nDescendant = esau\nDescendant = reuben\nDescendant = simeon\nDescendant = levi\nDescendant = judah</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 14,
        "code": "## Étape 6 : Compiler Parent en Bash\n\nPlace à la partie pratique — compilons nos faits `parent/2` en un script Bash !",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 15,
        "code": "% Charger le compilateur de flux\n\\+ \\+ (\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/stream_compiler)),\n\n    % Compiler les faits parent en bash\n    stream_compiler:compile_facts(parent, 2, [], _BashCode),\n    writeln('Generated Bash code for parent/2:'),\n    writeln(_BashCode)\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "source_sink `unifyweaver(core/stream_compiler)' does not exist",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">source_sink `unifyweaver(core/stream_compiler)' does not exist</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 16,
        "code": "## Étape 7 : Enregistrer le script de Parent\n\nEnregistrons le code Bash généré dans un fichier.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 17,
        "code": "% Enregistrer dans un fichier\n\\+ \\+ (\n    stream_compiler:compile_facts(parent, 2, [], _BashCode),\n    setup_call_cleanup(\n        open('../output/parent.sh', write, _Stream),\n        write(_Stream, _BashCode),\n        close(_Stream)),\n    writeln('Saved to ../output/parent.sh')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: stream_compiler:compile_facts/4",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: stream_compiler:compile_facts/4</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 18,
        "code": "## Étape 8 : Compiler Ancestor en Bash\n\nCompilons maintenant le prédicat `ancestor/2`, qui utilise la récursion.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 19,
        "code": "% Charger le compilateur récursif\n\\+ \\+ (\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)),\n\n    % Compiler ancestor en bash\n    compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [], _BashCode),\n    writeln('Generated Bash code for ancestor/2:'),\n    writeln(_BashCode)\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "source_sink `unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)' does not exist",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">source_sink `unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)' does not exist</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 20,
        "code": "## Étape 9 : Enregistrer le script d'Ancestor\n\nEnregistrez le script d'ancêtre dans un fichier.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 21,
        "code": "% Enregistrer dans un fichier\n\\+ \\+ (\n    compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [], _BashCode),\n    setup_call_cleanup(\n        open('../output/ancestor.sh', write, _Stream),\n        write(_Stream, _BashCode),\n        close(_Stream)),\n    writeln('Saved to ../output/ancestor.sh')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "'<meta-call>'/1: Unknown procedure: compile_recursive/3",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">'&lt;meta-call&gt;'/1: Unknown procedure: compile_recursive/3</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 22,
        "code": "## Étape 10 : Tester les scripts générés\n\nTestons maintenant nos scripts Bash générés ! Nous utiliserons la commande magique `%%bash` pour exécuter des commandes bash.",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
